cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Если вы используете ruSyntax в исследованиях или программах, пожалуйста, сошлитесь на библиотеку."
title: "ruSyntax, a fast dependency parser for Russian"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Shkarin
    given-names: Sergey
    email: kouki.sergey@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-19
repository-code: "https://github.com/SergeyShk/ruSyntax"
url: "https://sergeyshk.github.io/ruSyntax/"
license: MIT
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24384006
keywords:
  - russian
  - nlp
  - syntax
  - dependency parsing
  - universal dependencies
  - rust
abstract: "ruSyntax is a dependency parser of Russian with a Rust core and a Python API: for every word of a sentence it finds the head and the Universal Dependencies relation. A BiLSTM over the words, their endings and the ruMorph parts of speech and features scores the arcs with a biaffine scorer and builds the maximum spanning tree with one root, non-projective trees included; the relations are chosen by the pair of the dependent and its head. The model is trained on the Taiga, GSD and Poetry treebanks of UD 2.19, and its int8 weights are distributed under CC BY-SA 4.0. Raw text is split into sentences and words by the anySeg segmenter and tagged by the ruMorph morphological analyzer; sentences are parsed without the GIL."
